  "description": "BILWOK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H100 Cl8 Dy4 Mn8 N8 O54,4(C1 H4 O1),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.821-3.883 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.69-130.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H124Cl8Dy4Mn8N8O62. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Dy(III).",
